<title>BELGIUM: Solvay sees no fx impact on 1997 earnings.</title>
<headline>Solvay sees no fx impact on 1997 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian chemicals and drugs group Solvay said it expected recent currency developments to have no impact on earnings this year, noting the effect of a high dollar had been offset by the Thai baht.  </p>
<p>&quot;Gains on the dollar have compensated potential losses on net assets in Thai baht. At the level of exchange rates reached at end July the earnings of 1997 should therefore not be affected by currency changes,&quot; Solvay said in a statement on first half 1997 results.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
